==Restrictions==
Rarity: Only [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]] and [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]]

==Battleground==
*1 [[Condemned Peng]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*3 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 14.67 seconds<sup>440f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Li'l Macho Legs Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Macho Legs Cat]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Li'l Jamiera Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Jamiera Cat]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**8 [[Li'l Macho Legs Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Macho Legs Cats]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**2 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
**7 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage aims to threaten your units with both Waves from Li'l Macho Legs and Li'l Jamiera, and Surges from the Condemned Pengs and Sinner Snaches. The stage is on base hit, so you won't need a Rich Cat for this level.

If you own a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] (lvl 40+) and [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Mightycat]] (lvl 30+), you can easily 2-cycle the Li'l Jamiera. Just try to hit the base with Bahamut while also sending out a Mightycat, and then survive until both are back off cooldown, and do the same thing again. Li'l Jamiera should either die, or be very low on hp, and ready to be finished off by your other attackers, such as [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]].

===Recommended Units===
*[[Rugby Cat (Rare Cat)|Gridiron Cat]]: Extremely strong here, even at level 30. With both Wave and Surge Immune, as well as Strong vs. Aku, Gridiron is your main unit to use here.
*[[Calligraphy Cat (Rare Cat)|Tea Master Cat]]: Similarly to Gridiron, is both Wave and Surge Immune, although not as effective.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Dumpling's level 7 Wave allows him to use the Snaches or Aku Doges as a stepping stone to hit the whole battlefield.
*[[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]]: Emergency anti-Jamiera CC in case he's pushing too close to your base.
*Talented [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]]: Dancer has a high enough range to outrange Condemned Peng and has Wave Immune. He also outranges Li'l Jamiera, but only by 10 range, so protect him carefully.
*Talented Awakened Bahamut Cat: As stated above, Bahamut's raw damage allows you to get insane amounts of value here, highly damaging some of the Li'l Macho Legs as well as having Explosion to spread that damage to any Condemned Pengs.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando]]: Once again, Jagando is going to be your main backliner for these stages, having KB vs. Traitless for the Li'l Cats and having Surge Immunity for the Pengs and Snaches. Doesn't have Wave Immune though, so support him well with...
*[[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]]: Supercat can hit a Sinner Snache and not get juggled, leaving him as an immobile Wave Blocker for a few seconds. If you can't get that down, just use him to Weaken Li'l Jamiera so your Jagando lives longer.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]: Shreds this stage. With Wave Immunity, LD to hit Li'l Jamiera through the multiple stepping stones, and Massive vs. Traitless, Hitman will destroy both of the Li'l Cats here. Don't rely on him too much, as he's still vulnerable to Surges.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Storm Beast Naala]]: Naala has both Surge and Wave Immune in addition to decent generalist damage which helps in chipping Li'l Jamiera down.

